1
00:00:07,624 --> 00:01:07,562
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,076 --> 00:02:08,076
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

3
00:02:57,486 --> 00:03:01,936
Be careful, Osman.
I need you.

4
00:03:06,368 --> 00:03:11,278
Where are you going?
Where are you going? Come at me!

5
00:03:42,778 --> 00:03:46,778
You aren't alone, Osman Bey!

6
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:03,919
Who is that woman?

7
00:04:03,919 --> 00:04:07,919
Attack! Attack!

8
00:04:09,878 --> 00:04:12,988
Kill them!

9
00:04:32,453 --> 00:04:35,423
We are here, my bey!

10
00:04:58,962 --> 00:05:01,692
Kill them!

11
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:27,490
The lord! Osman Bey, catch the lord!

12
00:05:30,483 --> 00:05:34,483
Boran, Gencebay; help Bamsı Bey!

13
00:06:09,776 --> 00:06:13,776
-Are you all right, my bey?
-Kids...

14
00:06:14,556 --> 00:06:17,936
I'm all right, kids.

15
00:06:45,355 --> 00:06:49,355
Charge! It's the day of honor!

16
00:07:34,902 --> 00:07:38,902
My holy Allah, protect us.

17
00:07:48,809 --> 00:07:52,809
Lower your weapons!

18
00:07:53,871 --> 00:07:57,871
-Drop your weapons, Gündüz Bey!
-Hold!

19
00:07:58,327 --> 00:08:01,957
I told you to lower them!

20
00:08:02,199 --> 00:08:05,309
Hold!

21
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:15,440
Gündüz Bey.
Gündüz Bey!

22
00:08:15,575 --> 00:08:19,275
Lower it.

23
00:08:30,031 --> 00:08:32,981
Lower!

24
00:08:34,039 --> 00:08:39,130
Bring me a cart! Dündar Bey and
the women will come with me!

25
00:08:41,364 --> 00:08:45,364
If someone follows us, I'll kill
them all!

26
00:09:09,153 --> 00:09:13,153
Bring a cart!

27
00:09:28,011 --> 00:09:32,681
Charge! Charge!
Kill them!

28
00:10:19,347 --> 00:10:23,347
Who are you, woman?

29
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:46,976
Don't pollute your hands with the
blood of the heathen.

30
00:10:46,976 --> 00:10:51,036
The blood of the heathen can't
pollute anything of ours.

31
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:56,650
Honorable Ertuğrul Ghazi's son,
Osman Bey.

32
00:11:05,521 --> 00:11:07,767
My bey!

33
00:11:13,312 --> 00:11:16,222
My bey!

34
00:11:16,222 --> 00:11:20,222
-Are you all right, my bey?
-I'm all right.

35
00:11:20,222 --> 00:11:24,222
-How is Bamsı Bey?
-Gencebay took him, my bey.

36
00:11:26,252 --> 00:11:30,252
Will we go after Nikola?

37
00:11:31,350 --> 00:11:35,680
Even if he was lying,
we'll take our measures.

38
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,780
We'll be at the tribe at once.
Come on!

39
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:42,320
I will come with you.

40
00:11:45,896 --> 00:11:49,089
You haven't told me who you are, woman.

41
00:11:49,089 --> 00:11:53,529
Kızılbey's son Umur Bey's
daughter Malhun Hatun.

42
00:11:55,672 --> 00:11:59,132
We came for jihad.

43
00:11:59,132 --> 00:12:04,542
-Umur Bey's daughter, huh?
-He sent me as an envoy.

44
00:12:04,542 --> 00:12:08,542
We were destined to meet like this.

45
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:25,248
-Come on.
-My bey, Savcı Bey might be ambushed.

46
00:12:25,248 --> 00:12:30,038
This isn't the first time they are
ambushed. They can take care of it.

47
00:12:30,546 --> 00:12:33,026
Come on!

48
00:12:55,533 --> 00:13:00,843
You won't run away, Savcı Bey.
I will finish you here.

49
00:13:00,843 --> 00:13:04,843
Hang on, valiants.
Hang on!

50
00:13:04,843 --> 00:13:08,283
Our Allah will help us.

51
00:13:22,599 --> 00:13:27,989
We need to get out of here and go
to a cave. They can't stop us at night.

52
00:13:36,181 --> 00:13:38,661
Son!

53
00:13:58,942 --> 00:14:01,772
Come on.

54
00:14:14,327 --> 00:14:18,377
-Father!
-Daughter...

55
00:14:18,377 --> 00:14:23,327
-Is this how we meet, father?
-Allah is the one who decides.

56
00:14:23,327 --> 00:14:25,607
Be patient.

57
00:15:09,314 --> 00:15:12,354
Targun!

58
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:18,211
-Let her go!
-No one can stop me, Selcan Hatun.

59
00:15:19,915 --> 00:15:23,275
-I told you to let her go!
-Stop!

60
00:15:23,275 --> 00:15:27,275
Aunt, aunt, stop.

61
00:15:27,275 --> 00:15:31,202
What are you saying, Gündüz?

62
00:15:31,202 --> 00:15:35,612
Don't you see that they are taking
the women and Dündar?

63
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:45,840
They seized Osman's escrows!

64
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:51,340
-I will stop this!
-Aunt! Aunt!

65
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:56,260
They took our loved ones captive,
don't you see?

66
00:15:56,260 --> 00:16:02,330
-Do you want them to die? Don't.
-They can't do this!

67
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:07,670
-I won't let them. Move!
-Selcan Hatun!

68
00:16:09,909 --> 00:16:12,829
My sheik.

69
00:16:15,037 --> 00:16:21,277
My sheik, don't you see?
They have Osman's escrows.

70
00:16:25,642 --> 00:16:30,882
My sheik, they took Osman's wife
as a captive.

71
00:16:31,299 --> 00:16:35,959
She is my precious daughter, Selcan Hatun.

72
00:16:36,601 --> 00:16:40,921
Let us leave revenge to Osman Bey.

73
00:16:41,282 --> 00:16:45,282
We should be patient.

74
00:17:12,709 --> 00:17:14,949
Father...

75
00:17:16,337 --> 00:17:21,747
Göktuğ... Göktuğ!

76
00:17:21,747 --> 00:17:28,057
May you burn in hell, Göktuğ!
May you lose your hands!

77
00:17:28,101 --> 00:17:32,101
May you never live a happy day, Göktuğ!

78
00:19:19,415 --> 00:19:22,215
Bayhoca!

79
00:19:32,792 --> 00:19:37,208
I hope you've fulfilled your longing with
your son, Savcı.

80
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:40,788
This is the last time you see him.

81
00:19:40,788 --> 00:19:48,128
-Flatyos, I will kill you.
-Stop, son. That's what he wants.

82
00:19:49,124 --> 00:19:53,124
We must hang on until the
nightfall.

83
00:19:56,302 --> 00:20:00,302
Cerkutay! Cerkutay, where are you going?

84
00:21:07,373 --> 00:21:11,373
Come on, hurry!

85
00:21:41,404 --> 00:21:46,764
What happened? Where are you going,
Bala Hatun? Where?

86
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:50,259
-You'll stay with me here.
-What are you doing?

87
00:21:50,259 --> 00:21:55,099
What are you doing? Leave her,
take me!

88
00:21:55,106 --> 00:21:59,956
Shut up, I don't need you!
Bala is my guarantee.

89
00:21:59,956 --> 00:22:03,956
She'll come with me.

90
00:22:04,732 --> 00:22:09,472
-Let me go!
-Tell Osman Bey!

91
00:22:09,472 --> 00:22:14,582
I have his escrows!
Come on, hurry!

92
00:22:30,012 --> 00:22:34,012
You don't have a guarantee now, Targun.

93
00:22:37,282 --> 00:22:39,762
Come on!

94
00:23:33,598 --> 00:23:37,338
Flatyos!

95
00:23:37,530 --> 00:23:41,260
Don't move, I'm aiming!

96
00:23:45,545 --> 00:23:49,075
Soldiers, kill him!

97
00:23:50,161 --> 00:23:52,801
Come on, warriors!

98
00:23:56,041 --> 00:23:59,351
Baysungur, come!

99
00:24:22,551 --> 00:24:27,661
They are running away!
Soldiers, follow me!

100
00:25:04,517 --> 00:25:09,127
Are you happy? Have you taken
your revenge?

101
00:25:09,421 --> 00:25:13,421
What kind of a Turk are you, Göktuğ?

102
00:25:17,127 --> 00:25:22,127
Answer me, treacherous dog!

103
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:30,710
What happened, Bala? Did Osman
not come to rescue you?

104
00:25:31,577 --> 00:25:35,577
Or is he in a greater trouble now?

105
00:25:39,838 --> 00:25:44,898
You both will die today. You won't
see each other.

106
00:25:46,029 --> 00:25:50,029
The last thing you'll see will be
my face.

107
00:25:50,795 --> 00:25:54,795
How is it?
Did you like that?

108
00:26:19,482 --> 00:26:25,082
Savcı Bey! Savcı Bey!
We left Cerkutay behind!

109
00:26:27,914 --> 00:26:33,404
If we keep waiting, his sacrifice
will be for nothing! Come on!

110
00:26:33,585 --> 00:26:37,585
If they do something to him,
I'll skin them alive!

111
00:26:37,802 --> 00:26:41,342
Aygül, come on!

112
00:26:51,277 --> 00:26:54,737
Cerkutay doesn't die!

113
00:26:58,105 --> 00:27:01,695
We need to reach the cave, come on!

114
00:27:03,107 --> 00:27:06,017
Come on!

115
00:27:13,915 --> 00:27:18,455
Savcı! Don't run away!
Face me like a valiant!

116
00:27:39,381 --> 00:27:42,221
Oh, thank Allah!

117
00:27:47,029 --> 00:27:51,329
-Uncle? Are you all right?
-I'm fine. I'm fine. I'm fine.

118
00:27:51,329 --> 00:27:57,499
Gündüz Bey, they didn't leave Bala.
They also have Osman Bey's chests.

119
00:27:58,349 --> 00:28:04,459
It's true, my nephew. They have the
chests but save Bala first. Come on.

120
00:28:04,459 --> 00:28:06,622
-All right, uncle.
-Come on.

121
00:28:06,622 --> 00:28:12,026
The Alps will take you to the tribe.
We'll go and rescue Bala Hatun.

122
00:28:47,938 --> 00:28:51,938
Come on! Come down, hurry!

123
00:28:56,927 --> 00:29:00,317
Hurry, I said!

124
00:29:00,317 --> 00:29:02,557
Come on!

125
00:29:08,171 --> 00:29:13,911
-What are you waiting for? Hurry!
-Let me go!

126
00:29:20,512 --> 00:29:24,512
Come here, Bala!
Come on!

127
00:30:37,555 --> 00:30:40,065
Move!

128
00:30:54,135 --> 00:30:59,375
Look at you! I pity you.

129
00:30:59,375 --> 00:31:02,375
I hate you.

130
00:31:03,424 --> 00:31:07,424
I'll tear your ugly face apart.

131
00:31:09,959 --> 00:31:13,959
And you will watch it, is that so, Göktuğ?

132
00:31:15,094 --> 00:31:19,094
With pleasure.

133
00:31:23,522 --> 00:31:28,532
If you can't give an heir,
a son to your husband...

134
00:31:29,381 --> 00:31:33,971
...why would you live,
right, Bala?

135
00:31:46,494 --> 00:31:49,930
-Hurry!
-Come on!

136
00:32:07,142 --> 00:32:12,569
-What are you waiting for, hurry!
-Let me go!

137
00:33:10,292 --> 00:33:12,972
My bey!

138
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:45,761
-Boran Alp!
-Göktuğ! Brother!

139
00:34:52,027 --> 00:34:58,338
I knew you would do it. I knew
Osman Bey wouldn't discard you.

140
00:35:08,137 --> 00:35:13,527
-Are you all right, Bala?
-I'm all right.

141
00:35:24,190 --> 00:35:28,190
So, that's how you die?

142
00:35:36,629 --> 00:35:39,909
Bala.

143
00:35:58,606 --> 00:36:01,956
My bey.

144
00:36:11,466 --> 00:36:15,286
-My bey!
-Brother!

145
00:36:15,896 --> 00:36:21,456
-I missed you, my bey.
-Mashallah, Göktuğ.

146
00:36:21,698 --> 00:36:24,898
You did it.

147
00:36:25,449 --> 00:36:32,449
Now, you will lead the Cumans.

148
00:36:33,127 --> 00:36:37,127
We'll miss each other again, my bey.

149
00:36:37,127 --> 00:36:42,477
Until the victory, brother.
Until the victory.

150
00:36:46,452 --> 00:36:50,452
All right, my bey.

151
00:36:51,234 --> 00:36:56,374
-All right, Bala Hatun.
-May Allah bless you, Göktuğ.

152
00:37:00,219 --> 00:37:04,219
It's a good plan, Osman Bey.

153
00:37:06,159 --> 00:37:12,359
And it will continue.
Göktuğ...

154
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:18,150
...you should leave now.
-All right.

155
00:37:23,540 --> 00:37:29,380
One of the Ankara beys, Kızılbey's son
Umur Bey's daughter.

156
00:37:29,380 --> 00:37:35,130
My name is Malhun Hatun.
We are answering Osman Bey's call.

157
00:37:35,896 --> 00:37:39,236
Welcome.

158
00:37:42,230 --> 00:37:47,550
Bala, take care of the chests.

159
00:37:48,151 --> 00:37:51,471
Don't worry.

160
00:37:54,964 --> 00:37:58,964
Alps!

161
00:38:00,905 --> 00:38:04,905
Take Bala Hatun and Malhun Hatun
to the tribe.

162
00:38:08,493 --> 00:38:10,963
Come on, alps!

163
00:38:17,206 --> 00:38:23,826
Boran, we'll go to Söğüt and
find out about that caravan issue.

164
00:38:23,826 --> 00:38:26,546
All right, my bey.

165
00:38:30,767 --> 00:38:35,287
Come on, we must go to Söğüt
before they do.

166
00:39:15,936 --> 00:39:19,936
Let's see what the caravan owners
say.

167
00:40:00,892 --> 00:40:04,002
Alps.

168
00:40:08,741 --> 00:40:11,991
Untie them.

169
00:40:23,992 --> 00:40:30,392
Thank God. May Allah bless you, my bey.
Thank God.

170
00:40:35,171 --> 00:40:38,551
May Allah bless you, my bey.

171
00:40:39,594 --> 00:40:44,084
May Allah always keep you
on our head.

172
00:40:47,891 --> 00:40:52,641
-Take a breath.
-Thank you, brother.

173
00:40:52,641 --> 00:40:56,471
May Allah bless you, brothers.

174
00:40:56,778 --> 00:41:02,618
So, tell me now.
I'm listening to you.

175
00:41:02,618 --> 00:41:05,298
They raided our caravan, my bey.

176
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:11,300
We lost all our capital, my bey.

177
00:41:11,300 --> 00:41:16,190
They tortured us in Söğüt, my bey.

178
00:41:21,917 --> 00:41:27,387
-Then, why didn't they kill you?
-Because of our gold, my bey.

179
00:41:27,387 --> 00:41:32,667
They tortured us to make us tell
them where our gold is, my bey.

180
00:41:49,426 --> 00:41:55,696
For the traders, assets aren't
the shiver of life...

181
00:41:56,911 --> 00:42:01,851
...but life is the shiver of the assets.

182
00:42:10,490 --> 00:42:17,100
My bey, you told us to bring
a caravan...

183
00:42:17,100 --> 00:42:22,350
...and if you get hurt
in Söğüt, I have the responsibility.

184
00:42:22,364 --> 00:42:24,864
Süleyman...

185
00:42:28,329 --> 00:42:33,609
For that reason, we think that...

186
00:42:34,290 --> 00:42:38,290
...asking for compensation
is our right, my bey.

187
00:42:47,425 --> 00:42:53,415
If we gave our word.
It will be that way.

188
00:42:53,470 --> 00:42:56,850
Even if we die.

189
00:42:58,141 --> 00:43:03,443
-Thank you, my bey.
-May Allah bless you, my bey.

190
00:43:03,443 --> 00:43:08,746
But, the devil prepared dinner...

191
00:43:08,746 --> 00:43:13,206
...we should find out who is
sitting at the table first.

192
00:43:13,499 --> 00:43:18,589
Then, we'll take care of that.

193
00:43:18,749 --> 00:43:23,639
May Allah give you a long life, my bey.

194
00:43:25,252 --> 00:43:29,712
Same for all of us.

195
00:43:32,752 --> 00:43:35,402
All of us.

196
00:44:13,781 --> 00:44:18,831
We played our game.
But...

197
00:44:19,691 --> 00:44:23,691
Do you think he is suspicious?

198
00:44:24,273 --> 00:44:29,953
If he was suspicious,
you wouldn't be talking now.

199
00:44:31,430 --> 00:44:37,060
Despite everything, we should
keep our guard.

200
00:44:38,354 --> 00:44:42,354
If Osman woke up...

201
00:44:42,537 --> 00:44:47,447
...we must put him into sleep again.

202
00:45:11,678 --> 00:45:14,918
Watch them.

203
00:45:15,098 --> 00:45:19,098
Thank you.

204
00:45:25,144 --> 00:45:28,714
Thank you.

205
00:45:37,251 --> 00:45:43,561
-So, you are Umur Bey's daughter?
-Yes, Selcan Hatun. Do you know my father?

206
00:45:43,777 --> 00:45:48,787
Everyone knows Umur Bey in Anatolia.

207
00:45:50,818 --> 00:45:56,048
You suffered so much from the Mongols.

208
00:45:56,642 --> 00:46:00,127
Ever since I remember, we are moving
from here and there.

209
00:46:00,127 --> 00:46:00,192
Geyhatu is attacking us over and over.
Ever since I remember, we are moving
from here and there.

210
00:46:00,192 --> 00:46:03,607
Geyhatu is attacking us over and over.

211
00:46:03,814 --> 00:46:10,151
My Lord's compassion and the saints'
hope are with the ones who are oppressed.

212
00:46:10,151 --> 00:46:15,621
Inshallah. May our Lord and the saints
show mercy on us.

213
00:46:15,994 --> 00:46:18,014
We are breathing thanks to our Lord.

214
00:46:18,073 --> 00:46:22,533
May Allah praise my grandfather
Imurin Mayesefettin.

215
00:46:27,279 --> 00:46:29,729
Ahmet what's going on?

216
00:46:29,820 --> 00:46:31,830
Don't reveal my place.

217
00:46:33,405 --> 00:46:35,185
Ahmet!

218
00:46:35,300 --> 00:46:37,030
Okay.

219
00:46:46,481 --> 00:46:51,741
My Bala, my beautful daughter.
We were chatting with Malhun Hatun.

220
00:46:57,305 --> 00:46:59,855
What are you doing here?

221
00:47:00,051 --> 00:47:04,131
I'm looking for Ahmet, mother.
Have you seen him?

222
00:47:04,636 --> 00:47:09,596
No, daughter.
Ahmet is not here.

223
00:47:11,079 --> 00:47:12,979
Okay then.

224
00:47:15,975 --> 00:47:20,155
It looks like we were destined to meet
in the wrong time, Malhun Hatun.

225
00:47:23,017 --> 00:47:27,217
I am going to be a guest of yours
if you approve, Bala Hatun.

226
00:47:27,505 --> 00:47:30,445
I hope better days are waiting for us.

227
00:47:32,778 --> 00:47:37,658
Now that you are our guest,
you are welcomed.

228
00:47:52,074 --> 00:47:56,034
- I won! Now you run!
- Hey, son.

229
00:47:57,256 --> 00:48:00,286
Go now, I'll join you.

230
00:48:04,039 --> 00:48:08,519
Was that your son?
He is so sweet, Masha Allah.

231
00:48:09,550 --> 00:48:13,280
No.
He is not my own.

232
00:48:16,704 --> 00:48:21,834
He is all of ours.
He is an orphan.

233
00:48:23,421 --> 00:48:25,441
His parents are martyred.

234
00:48:35,296 --> 00:48:38,216
May my Lord praise him.

235
00:48:39,995 --> 00:48:42,315
- Amin.
- Amin.

236
00:48:46,859 --> 00:48:50,279
I want to go to my Alps,
if you excuse me.

237
00:48:50,339 --> 00:48:53,709
Of course, daughter.

238
00:49:03,918 --> 00:49:05,358
My Bala.

239
00:49:09,800 --> 00:49:12,210
What are you thinking?

240
00:49:14,611 --> 00:49:19,751
We know who she is. but we don't know
why she is here. Selcan Mother.

241
00:49:23,811 --> 00:49:26,301
Isn't it obvious, my daughter?

242
00:49:27,484 --> 00:49:32,734
The aimless ones don't have a path.
They can't succeed.

243
00:49:33,932 --> 00:49:38,374
- It's not our business from now on.
- Yes.

244
00:49:40,064 --> 00:49:43,344
She is going to talk to our Bey
about why she has come.

245
00:49:46,541 --> 00:49:50,231
Saints say "Children are father's mirror"

246
00:49:50,231 --> 00:49:53,711
Apparently she is valiant like her father.

247
00:49:53,733 --> 00:49:57,838
Her father Umur Bey was a very
important Bey, my daughter.

248
00:49:57,838 --> 00:50:05,858
His tribe immigrated from Ankara,
from Germiyan.

249
00:50:06,961 --> 00:50:11,331
Let's see now where they are going to
land.

250
00:50:17,145 --> 00:50:20,672
It's all because of me. Bamsi Bey.

251
00:50:20,672 --> 00:50:23,642
I shouldn't have listened to you.

252
00:50:24,597 --> 00:50:27,677
What were you supposed to do then?

253
00:50:43,269 --> 00:50:47,541
Don't tire yourself Bamsi Bey, sit.

254
00:50:47,541 --> 00:50:49,611
He doesn't listen at all, my Bey.

255
00:50:52,676 --> 00:50:55,756
He tried to pray in this situation.

256
00:51:08,734 --> 00:51:10,744
Bamsi Bey.

257
00:51:13,461 --> 00:51:16,181
How did we fall into this trap?

258
00:51:18,236 --> 00:51:22,916
We couldn't find the betrayers
in the tribe yet.

259
00:51:24,509 --> 00:51:27,529
We are going to find him finally.

260
00:51:27,850 --> 00:51:32,700
We are going to bait him to
wolves.

261
00:51:33,811 --> 00:51:37,421
But I need to see Governor Yorga.

262
00:51:40,692 --> 00:51:45,692
Only he can save us from Nicola.

263
00:51:51,393 --> 00:51:57,993
Idris Bey, excuse us.
We have a private issue with Bamsi Bey.

264
00:51:58,214 --> 00:52:02,774
Of course my Bey. I am leaving.
You go on.

265
00:52:02,983 --> 00:52:08,023
Bamsi Bey, if there is anything you
need. I'm right outside.

266
00:52:18,681 --> 00:52:25,531
Osman Bey, Idris Bey has heard that
you are going to meet Governor Yorga.

267
00:52:27,968 --> 00:52:32,178
I am about to find the betrayer,
Bamsi Bey.

268
00:52:35,166 --> 00:52:40,486
- Let's see if Nicola hears about this.
- You are suspicious of Idris.

269
00:52:41,680 --> 00:52:46,600
- I already suspected him.
- Me too.

270
00:52:51,090 --> 00:52:53,800
We are going to find out,

271
00:52:58,819 --> 00:53:02,839
My Brother Gunduz, Abdurrahman Ghazi and
alps are on their way.

272
00:53:04,483 --> 00:53:07,183
We haven't heard from my brother Savci yet.

273
00:53:07,407 --> 00:53:09,777
Aygul is with them also.

274
00:53:11,034 --> 00:53:12,774
Apparently...

275
00:53:15,248 --> 00:53:18,358
They took Vladius' bait.

276
00:53:20,959 --> 00:53:23,949
Don't worry, Osman Bey.

277
00:53:24,506 --> 00:53:28,806
Cerkutay and Aygul are with them.

278
00:53:30,107 --> 00:53:32,637
Yes, Bamsi Bey, yes.

279
00:53:32,905 --> 00:53:39,215
Let me go to my Sheik now.
I see you well, Masha Allah.

280
00:53:39,452 --> 00:53:44,052
Eyvallah, eyvallah (thank you) Osman Bey.
Take my greetings to him.

281
00:53:44,077 --> 00:53:47,298
As soon as I become alright, I'll visit
him too.

282
00:53:47,298 --> 00:53:49,198
Eyvallah(okay) Bamsi Bey.

283
00:53:49,424 --> 00:53:51,554
Eyvallah.

284
00:54:24,553 --> 00:54:26,853
Hello Gonca Hatun.

285
00:54:27,672 --> 00:54:29,702
Thank you.

286
00:54:32,088 --> 00:54:34,328
What are these?

287
00:54:34,554 --> 00:54:38,444
I am organizing the provisions
for Sogut.

288
00:54:38,953 --> 00:54:44,633
Thanks to Bala Hatun, the ones who are in
need will get these.

289
00:54:45,069 --> 00:54:47,019
May Allah praise her.

290
00:54:50,087 --> 00:54:53,087
May Allah praise you too, Boran.

291
00:54:53,580 --> 00:54:58,670
I heard that you saved Bala from those
bandits,

292
00:55:00,049 --> 00:55:04,349
- If it wasn't for you...
- Thanks to our Bey, Gonca Hatun.

293
00:55:11,736 --> 00:55:16,046
Gonca Hatun, what are you doing.
You are going to hurt yourself.

294
00:55:16,676 --> 00:55:22,417
Do you think I'm such an easy girl?

295
00:55:43,631 --> 00:55:46,321
I know you are not easy.

296
00:55:46,547 --> 00:55:51,517
But if you get hurt, I get hurt.

297
00:56:19,399 --> 00:56:22,699
Speed up, Boran Bey.

298
00:56:23,350 --> 00:56:26,020
There are lots of things to do.

299
00:57:13,730 --> 00:57:16,060
Thank you Hatuns.

300
00:57:38,296 --> 00:57:42,826
Everything is ready.
You can take your rest.

301
00:57:43,113 --> 00:57:48,233
- Are the tents for my Alps ready?
- Sure. They are all our guests.

302
00:58:02,381 --> 00:58:04,461
Is there a problem?

303
00:58:05,850 --> 00:58:11,720
Your Hatuns weave rugs. carpets.
Right?

304
00:58:11,977 --> 00:58:13,847
True.

305
00:58:16,337 --> 00:58:18,517
Why are you asking?

306
00:58:19,971 --> 00:58:22,171
I liked the cloth in Damascus.

307
00:58:23,819 --> 00:58:27,019
These are fine as well.

308
00:58:29,103 --> 00:58:36,403
Our Hatuns are the best when it comes to
being dexterous.

309
00:58:38,548 --> 00:58:44,818
The world is large, Bala Hatun.
You need to travel to know that.

310
00:58:53,638 --> 00:58:59,078
So you and your Bey couldn't find a
place to stay.

311
00:58:59,744 --> 00:59:01,894
I don't have a Bey(husband)

312
00:59:02,976 --> 00:59:05,046
Why?

313
00:59:07,355 --> 00:59:09,515
I am waiting for someone to show up.

314
00:59:11,618 --> 00:59:17,258
The world is large, Malhan Hatun.
I am sure you'll find someone.

315
00:59:19,893 --> 00:59:22,193
You keep looking.

316
00:59:29,750 --> 00:59:32,360
Don't worry Bala Hatun.

317
00:59:33,399 --> 00:59:36,919
My Bey is going to be a son of Bey.

318
00:59:37,238 --> 00:59:40,588
I am sure he'll find this daughter of Bey
someday.

319
00:59:52,751 --> 00:59:55,351
Good night.

320
01:00:35,077 --> 01:00:37,077
Here you sit, my sheik.

321
01:00:37,216 --> 01:00:40,726
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate)

322
01:00:45,970 --> 01:00:51,747
We have been looking forward to
seeing you. You honored our tribe.

323
01:00:51,747 --> 01:00:54,917
- Thank you.
- Of course, my Bey.

324
01:00:55,780 --> 01:01:02,690
Thank Allah that I get to see Ertugrul
Ghazi's son Osman Bey.

325
01:01:03,892 --> 01:01:05,542
Amin.

326
01:01:06,092 --> 01:01:10,222
We witness that you follow the path
of religion and traditions.

327
01:01:10,821 --> 01:01:13,131
May you be blessed.

328
01:01:13,152 --> 01:01:14,772
Amin my sheik.

329
01:01:25,055 --> 01:01:27,002
Can I, father?

330
01:01:27,002 --> 01:01:28,692
Of course.

331
01:01:30,719 --> 01:01:33,499
Come here.

332
01:01:46,344 --> 01:01:50,464
Be righteous like you are ordered to be.

333
01:01:50,914 --> 01:01:55,074
Don't let them pervert you and
tell them this:

334
01:01:55,234 --> 01:01:59,864
"I believed in Allah's book...

335
01:02:00,526 --> 01:02:04,586
and I was ordered to bring justice
to you."

336
01:02:06,565 --> 01:02:10,115
Allah says this in his book.

337
01:02:12,444 --> 01:02:18,394
And Hadrat Ayse said this:

338
01:02:19,415 --> 01:02:22,375
Whoever is the leader of a
community...

339
01:02:24,559 --> 01:02:29,249
he should be judicious...

340
01:02:30,020 --> 01:02:32,320
so that his way shall be enlightened.

341
01:02:34,014 --> 01:02:38,614
and if someone doesn't care
about justice...

342
01:02:40,849 --> 01:02:45,989
while he is in charge...

343
01:02:47,073 --> 01:02:50,003
his way shall be dark.

344
01:02:52,344 --> 01:02:56,968
May your way be clear, my Bey.

345
01:02:57,498 --> 01:03:00,458
May Allah bless your generation.

346
01:03:00,549 --> 01:03:03,022
- Amin.
- Amin.

347
01:03:03,022 --> 01:03:07,852
Turk's and Islam's dagger stabbed
on Byzantine.

348
01:03:08,365 --> 01:03:14,505
May my Allah let your children
to take your throne which...

349
01:03:14,951 --> 01:03:19,291
My Ancestor Ertugrul Ghazi
left for you...

350
01:03:21,488 --> 01:03:23,418
Amin my sheik.

351
01:03:25,420 --> 01:03:27,340
Amin.

352
01:04:24,813 --> 01:04:26,953
Don't shout for nothing.

353
01:04:26,993 --> 01:04:29,323
It hurts.

354
01:04:49,908 --> 01:04:53,108
Now it really hurts.

355
01:05:18,499 --> 01:05:21,219
Why are you looking like that?

356
01:05:23,773 --> 01:05:29,533
It shines like that when moonlight shines
on your sword.

357
01:05:31,995 --> 01:05:33,675
Like what?

358
01:05:37,259 --> 01:05:39,599
Like your eyes.

359
01:05:50,586 --> 01:05:53,916
Baysungur.
Try again.

360
01:05:53,965 --> 01:05:56,705
Okay my Bey.

361
01:06:22,085 --> 01:06:24,245
They are still waiting, my Bey.

362
01:06:25,511 --> 01:06:28,511
They are trying to leave us hungry and
dehydrated.

363
01:06:28,923 --> 01:06:31,453
We need to get out of here.

364
01:06:31,662 --> 01:06:34,762
- We have to take revenge for Dumrul.
- My Bey...

365
01:06:34,853 --> 01:06:37,683
If they hadn't had a crossbow...

366
01:06:38,368 --> 01:06:41,337
we could escape in the darkness.

367
01:06:41,337 --> 01:06:44,087
True, Baysungur.

368
01:06:44,593 --> 01:06:46,473
True.

369
01:06:51,135 --> 01:06:53,015
What's it now?

370
01:07:14,751 --> 01:07:18,991
I surrounded them like spider web.

371
01:07:19,391 --> 01:07:22,021
But Osman got away again.

372
01:07:22,319 --> 01:07:26,979
Your spiders are bad at netting.

373
01:07:28,850 --> 01:07:33,060
I was about to kill him, Petrus...
That woman...

374
01:07:34,050 --> 01:07:37,660
came out suddenly with her alps.

375
01:07:38,017 --> 01:07:40,434
Like she dropped out of sky.

376
01:07:40,434 --> 01:07:42,324
Which woman?

377
01:07:42,590 --> 01:07:45,580
Malhun Hatun!
Malhun Hatun!

378
01:07:52,364 --> 01:07:55,174
Malhun Hatun.

379
01:07:57,174 --> 01:07:59,074
I know her name.

380
01:07:59,584 --> 01:08:02,424
I don't know her...

381
01:08:02,883 --> 01:08:04,370
yet.

382
01:08:04,370 --> 01:08:07,270
She is Umur Bey's daughter.

383
01:08:07,292 --> 01:08:09,242
Who is Umur Bey?

384
01:08:09,303 --> 01:08:13,804
He is one of the strongest Beys of
Oghuz Turkmens around Ankara.

385
01:08:13,804 --> 01:08:19,542
Damn vandals! They scattered into our
lands like grasshoppers.

386
01:08:19,542 --> 01:08:23,062
What is Ankara Turkmen's daughter
doing here?

387
01:08:23,549 --> 01:08:30,219
She is doing Whatever Ertugrul did
and whatever Osman is doing here!

388
01:08:32,371 --> 01:08:39,865
Her grandfather Seyfettin Kızıl was one of
the Beys Sultan Aladdin trusted the most.

389
01:08:39,865 --> 01:08:44,325
But when Aladdin died, Seyfettin's son...

390
01:08:44,426 --> 01:08:50,996
rioted new Sultan Gıyasettin and Mongols.

391
01:08:52,197 --> 01:08:56,457
Genghis' dogs killed him in Kirsehir
at the end.

392
01:08:56,479 --> 01:09:02,160
Since then, they have had a feud
with Mongols.

393
01:09:02,942 --> 01:09:09,921
They are going to form an alliance with
Osman in order to defeat Geyhatu.

394
01:09:10,805 --> 01:09:14,345
So he sent his daughter.

395
01:09:18,416 --> 01:09:27,866
Bravo Nicola, Bravo.
I'll tell how wise you are to Pope.

396
01:09:35,100 --> 01:09:39,761
So that conquer Osman was planning
has started.

397
01:09:40,399 --> 01:09:47,189
We are going to wake up with their sheep's
bell, not our Church's bell!

398
01:09:47,376 --> 01:09:54,206
And Pope is not able to have the documents
he needs in order to locate Turk Boys..

399
01:09:54,206 --> 01:09:58,268
Because of your stupid actions!

400
01:10:04,597 --> 01:10:09,501
Tell me my sheik.
Over the seven seas, what is the...

401
01:10:09,501 --> 01:10:15,081
situation of Turks and Islam?

402
01:10:16,701 --> 01:10:24,291
We are like what we deserve.
Muslim attack Muslims, Turk attacks Turks.

403
01:10:25,295 --> 01:10:29,775
The arrow of Muslims aim other Muslims.

404
01:10:29,860 --> 01:10:34,520
The sword of Muslims rise against
other Muslims.

405
01:10:35,340 --> 01:10:39,430
Damascus is miserable.
Baghdad is blasted.

406
01:10:39,531 --> 01:10:44,771
Aleppo is miserable too.
And so is Anatolia.

407
01:10:45,855 --> 01:10:51,205
There is no government, no regulation.

408
01:10:52,302 --> 01:10:59,952
I have seen such places that people
want to die, my Bey.

409
01:11:01,588 --> 01:11:07,988
They think they are Sultans, Governors.

410
01:11:09,699 --> 01:11:17,739
If you can't unite, even golden throne
can't save your state, my Bey.

411
01:11:18,805 --> 01:11:24,175
The lasting thing is not the throne,
but the state.

412
01:11:26,355 --> 01:11:31,565
- What is going to happen?
- We'll see.

413
01:11:38,859 --> 01:11:41,069
You tell me.

414
01:11:42,683 --> 01:11:53,403
I'm working for my grandfather Suleiman
Shah and my father Ertugrul Ghazi's bequest

415
01:11:54,945 --> 01:11:58,405
What is their bequest, son?

416
01:11:58,499 --> 01:12:04,133
The blood, shedding from Erzurum highlands
to Aleppo deserts...

417
01:12:04,133 --> 01:12:09,463
want a glorious state.

418
01:12:10,480 --> 01:12:13,770
Sure, son. sure.

419
01:12:14,546 --> 01:12:22,436
This is what the world of Islam and
Turks are waiting for.

420
01:12:24,645 --> 01:12:28,265
Like a rooted tree sprouting from
its trunk...

421
01:12:30,244 --> 01:12:36,784
A glorious state that all the oppressed
ones can take shelter under it.

422
01:12:37,697 --> 01:12:40,385
This is what we are working on.

423
01:12:40,385 --> 01:12:45,785
We invite all Turkish tribes running
away from Mongols.

424
01:12:45,853 --> 01:12:50,963
This is all I am working for.

425
01:12:52,154 --> 01:12:57,894
The wisest Ahis in Anatolia are
in my land.

426
01:12:57,895 --> 01:13:04,315
The soldiers who want to battle madly
are in my army.

427
01:13:05,239 --> 01:13:14,049
Our Hatuns with swords in their belt
are more willing to battle than their men.

428
01:13:15,892 --> 01:13:21,052
They'll come.
You'll accommodate them.

429
01:13:22,127 --> 01:13:28,087
You'll give them grassland.
You'll give them home.

430
01:13:31,217 --> 01:13:34,397
- I'll kill Targun with my own...
- Of course.

431
01:13:34,908 --> 01:13:39,888
I can resurrect her for you to
kill her twice.

432
01:13:47,358 --> 01:13:50,723
We couldn't get the documents, right.

433
01:13:50,723 --> 01:13:54,543
But we know what Osman wants to do.
Don't we?

434
01:13:56,000 --> 01:14:02,410
Turkmen tribes are scattered all around
in Anatolia, running away from Mongols.

435
01:14:03,179 --> 01:14:08,151
Osman wants to have them, inviting them
to join him.

436
01:14:08,151 --> 01:14:14,571
He will give them the lands he took
from us!

437
01:14:15,967 --> 01:14:20,677
So you now realize Osman will promise
your lands to...

438
01:14:21,107 --> 01:14:27,487
Other Turkish tribes in order to
make them join him.

439
01:14:27,580 --> 01:14:30,930
Great.
Excellent.

440
01:14:35,902 --> 01:14:41,662
But the real question is that:

441
01:14:43,142 --> 01:14:50,945
You, Governor Nicola, what is
your plan against Osman?

442
01:15:03,545 --> 01:15:07,065
I'll do what I have to do

443
01:15:11,406 --> 01:15:18,736
Ahi will produce, soldiers will fight
the infidels.

444
01:15:18,891 --> 01:15:21,531
Hatuns will support.

445
01:15:21,928 --> 01:15:25,578
We'll grow together.

446
01:15:27,154 --> 01:15:33,454
This had always been like that
until mongols came, son.

447
01:15:34,588 --> 01:15:40,088
Think of your ancestor Hadrat
Keykubat Khan.

448
01:15:40,245 --> 01:15:44,005
He conquered Alaiye and Sinop.

449
01:15:44,915 --> 01:15:48,535
He united Mediterranean and
Black sea.

450
01:15:49,612 --> 01:15:56,422
He united everyone in his palace.

451
01:15:57,430 --> 01:16:03,470
He protected oppressed ones,
all the Turkmens.

452
01:16:05,969 --> 01:16:11,679
He established medical centers.

453
01:16:11,921 --> 01:16:17,051
He established schools.

454
01:16:18,162 --> 01:16:22,042
His courts were judicious.

455
01:16:23,216 --> 01:16:27,666
Inshallah my sheik.

456
01:16:28,057 --> 01:16:32,757
Our will in our hearts...

457
01:16:34,012 --> 01:16:36,582
are all for our state.

458
01:16:37,904 --> 01:16:42,634
Ahis, valiants, and Hatuns.

459
01:16:42,945 --> 01:16:49,955
There is one more class. Of course you
can establish a state with those, too.

460
01:16:50,024 --> 01:16:53,884
But it's unclear that it becomes
everlasting.

461
01:16:56,204 --> 01:16:59,198
Saints are necessary.

462
01:16:59,198 --> 01:17:04,278
Ahis, Ghazis, Hatuns.

463
01:17:05,744 --> 01:17:08,284
And Dervishes.

464
01:17:09,969 --> 01:17:15,349
You should know that dervishes
are also necessary.

465
01:17:17,078 --> 01:17:20,128
Dervishes bless you.

466
01:17:22,656 --> 01:17:27,116
My grandfather Gark...

467
01:17:27,278 --> 01:17:32,238
My grandfather Hayrani...

468
01:17:33,229 --> 01:17:39,479
Hunkar Bektas from Karacahoyuk...

469
01:17:39,834 --> 01:17:45,144
they all pray for you.

470
01:17:47,186 --> 01:17:52,486
And my father Taptuk prays for you too.

471
01:17:54,848 --> 01:17:57,778
I appreciate their prays.

472
01:17:58,522 --> 01:18:03,992
I got to see your face.

473
01:18:05,592 --> 01:18:09,362
I heard that you became Bey.

474
01:18:12,021 --> 01:18:16,591
I have a gift for you.

475
01:18:16,816 --> 01:18:19,722
I really appreciate it.

476
01:18:19,722 --> 01:18:23,482
You should take it.

477
01:18:24,484 --> 01:18:26,634
Gifts are to be taken.

478
01:18:26,770 --> 01:18:32,870
Your gift is a verse from Dervish Yunus.

479
01:18:36,778 --> 01:18:43,208
"Our state lives long thanks to these
saints we have and will have"

480
01:18:44,461 --> 01:18:49,501
Dervishes are wise, think about this.

481
01:18:50,244 --> 01:18:55,974
The verses of Dervish Yunus
make you think eventually.

482
01:18:56,792 --> 01:19:02,012
I hope you take the meaning out
of this verse, son.

483
01:19:03,137 --> 01:19:09,767
State is dervishes' breath and dervishes
becomes breath to the state.

484
01:19:17,676 --> 01:19:20,626
You warmed me.

485
01:19:20,801 --> 01:19:23,191
You enlightened me my sheik.

486
01:19:25,388 --> 01:19:35,298
Insha Allah the new state of Turks and
Islam becomes breath for dervishes.

487
01:19:37,959 --> 01:19:40,679
Elhamdulillah ( thanks to Allah).

488
01:19:46,983 --> 01:19:49,483
Ah Cerkutay Ah!

489
01:19:49,857 --> 01:19:52,987
Why are you leaving without informing
anyone!?

490
01:19:53,270 --> 01:19:54,950
What kind of horse is this?

491
01:19:57,439 --> 01:20:00,069
Ah you mad boy!

492
01:20:03,275 --> 01:20:05,775
Where is he already?

493
01:20:10,710 --> 01:20:13,480
Cerkutay is coming!

494
01:20:18,112 --> 01:20:20,362
Where have you been?

495
01:20:21,042 --> 01:20:26,412
We got the crossbow, and of course
the owner of this.

496
01:20:28,319 --> 01:20:29,829
What is this?

497
01:20:53,728 --> 01:20:55,198
My Bey.

498
01:21:01,457 --> 01:21:03,937
Cerkutay can't be hungry.

499
01:21:03,993 --> 01:21:09,323
Okay let's eat, you need to
gather your strength.

500
01:21:09,420 --> 01:21:13,400
Baysungur, go eat.

501
01:21:30,082 --> 01:21:32,192
My Bey.

502
01:21:33,095 --> 01:21:35,045
You are welcome.

503
01:21:40,053 --> 01:21:42,943
My Allah, give me patience.

504
01:21:52,852 --> 01:21:55,772
Eyvallah son.
(thank you)

505
01:21:57,421 --> 01:22:00,661
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( In the name of Allah, The Most Gracious and The Most Merciful)

506
01:22:02,402 --> 01:22:05,202
Eyvallah. (thanks)

507
01:22:31,104 --> 01:22:35,104
Can I come, my Hanım?

508
01:22:42,628 --> 01:22:47,308
How are my Alps?
- We are settled.

509
01:22:47,308 --> 01:22:51,308
- Do you need anything?
- No, my Hanım.

510
01:22:52,065 --> 01:22:59,465
As I said, you keep your eyes open,
keep your mouth shut.

511
01:23:00,159 --> 01:23:04,264
I want to know what happens in
here and in Sogut.

512
01:23:04,264 --> 01:23:06,684
Of course, my Hanım.

513
01:23:18,970 --> 01:23:23,660
It's time to talk to Osman Bey.

514
01:24:15,014 --> 01:24:19,544
Come on Dundar Bey.
This is not good.

515
01:24:20,108 --> 01:24:23,788
- Let's eat something.
- No Hatun.

516
01:24:24,432 --> 01:24:30,392
I don't want to eat. It's not time
to eat.

517
01:24:33,633 --> 01:24:35,023
I know.

518
01:24:37,587 --> 01:24:45,937
Even if you cooperated with that infidel,
Osman is still sitting on his throne.

519
01:24:47,805 --> 01:24:55,535
But there is no way back, Dündar Bey.

520
01:24:56,931 --> 01:25:03,311
When a wolf reveals himself, he cannot
go back, he must fight.

521
01:25:04,385 --> 01:25:05,875
He must.

522
01:25:06,200 --> 01:25:10,740
You are right, Hatun, but...

523
01:25:11,212 --> 01:25:16,032
What are we going to do with the
troubles that wolf encounters?

524
01:25:18,603 --> 01:25:22,003
Potter Idris...

525
01:25:24,299 --> 01:25:27,089
he knows everything.

526
01:25:28,688 --> 01:25:34,568
That I cooperated with Governor Nicola,
I helped them to raid the tribe.

527
01:25:35,041 --> 01:25:36,871
He knows everything.

528
01:25:40,614 --> 01:25:44,604
What are you talking about my Bey?
How did he learn this?

529
01:25:46,581 --> 01:25:52,261
It's not the case. From now on,
every breath the Potter takes...

530
01:25:52,290 --> 01:25:57,820
tightens the rope Osman Bey whipped
on my neck.

531
01:25:58,417 --> 01:26:01,617
What is your plan?

532
01:26:04,454 --> 01:26:09,354
My plan is to get rid of him.

533
01:26:25,411 --> 01:26:29,661
My dearie Bala...

534
01:26:30,903 --> 01:26:32,803
Every people has a challenge.

535
01:26:35,123 --> 01:26:39,210
Our love's challenge is this, my Bala.

536
01:26:39,210 --> 01:26:44,280
We obey whatever our Allah orders.

537
01:26:48,240 --> 01:26:50,478
I'll have a new Hatun.

538
01:26:54,148 --> 01:26:56,368
This time for real.

539
01:28:03,883 --> 01:28:05,833
Bala.

540
01:28:07,415 --> 01:28:10,665
What are you brooding on?

541
01:28:16,007 --> 01:28:20,867
One trouble ends, another one starts
my Osman.

542
01:28:24,567 --> 01:28:28,027
My path is like your hair.

543
01:28:29,970 --> 01:28:35,480
sometimes knotty, sometimes straggly.

544
01:28:37,687 --> 01:28:41,237
I love it in every shape.

545
01:28:42,262 --> 01:28:47,642
My Bala, my heart is in the darkness
of your hair.

546
01:28:48,464 --> 01:28:51,854
So you accept your troubles.

547
01:28:52,261 --> 01:28:57,991
If your eyes were troubling,
if your lips were poisonous...

548
01:28:59,000 --> 01:29:04,490
I'd still accept anything that comes
from you.

549
01:29:24,407 --> 01:29:27,617
Can I, Osman Bey?

550
01:29:44,551 --> 01:29:47,541
Let me check this Hatun.

551
01:30:29,381 --> 01:30:31,501
Come!

552
01:30:38,176 --> 01:30:40,766
What's it about, Malhun Hatun.

553
01:30:43,406 --> 01:30:46,606
Osman Bey I have a question for you.

554
01:30:51,179 --> 01:30:54,729
- Couldn't you wait until morning?
- My father is waiting for an answer.

555
01:31:02,475 --> 01:31:03,951
What's it?

556
01:31:03,951 --> 01:31:07,725
Osman Bey, we came here with your
invitation.

557
01:31:07,725 --> 01:31:10,692
We are here to shed blood, we are here
to die.

558
01:31:10,692 --> 01:31:15,262
But we saw a raided tribe,
captured Hatuns.

559
01:31:19,151 --> 01:31:23,818
- We didn't ask for your help Malhun Hatun.
- Osman Bey, this is not our issue.

560
01:31:23,818 --> 01:31:28,378
We are going to settle here, our destiny
is up to you.

561
01:31:28,502 --> 01:31:34,033
But we are not coming with five tents.
We have ten thousand men.

562
01:31:34,033 --> 01:31:36,953
You can't even count.

563
01:31:41,444 --> 01:31:46,684
It's my father Umur Bey's question,
forgive me. Don't shoot the messenger.

564
01:31:47,714 --> 01:31:53,064
But, tell me Osman Bey.
Can you handle that?

565
01:32:03,585 --> 01:32:07,055
It's not the right time or
place to talk about it.

566
01:34:13,852 --> 01:34:15,442
Welcome.

567
01:34:19,839 --> 01:34:22,569
I have things to tell Efendi Petrus.

568
01:34:59,622 --> 01:35:02,392
O, the Holy heart of Jesus...

569
01:35:02,858 --> 01:35:06,858
the infinite center of love...

570
01:35:08,421 --> 01:35:12,661
the infinite ocean of grace...

571
01:35:12,855 --> 01:35:15,595
the consolation of broken-hearted...

572
01:35:20,610 --> 01:35:23,220
the shelter of sinners....

573
01:35:30,633 --> 01:35:33,863
and the hope of the world.

574
01:36:31,968 --> 01:36:37,848
None of us is attached to Jesus like you.

575
01:36:38,273 --> 01:36:40,303
My brother Petrus.

576
01:36:56,878 --> 01:37:00,448
How can we expect good things...

577
01:37:03,026 --> 01:37:06,616
when we betray him like that?

578
01:37:23,854 --> 01:37:27,334
Ever since I came to Osman's lands...

579
01:37:28,073 --> 01:37:32,363
I haven't heard any good news.

580
01:37:33,668 --> 01:37:37,668
Then you'll love what you'll hear.

581
01:37:39,087 --> 01:37:44,937
Osman made an alliance
agreement with Yorgo.

582
01:37:45,744 --> 01:37:49,434
I thought Nikola should know.

583
01:37:56,270 --> 01:38:02,050
Then tell Nikola about this news.

584
01:38:02,094 --> 01:38:03,094
David.

585
01:38:04,478 --> 01:38:08,478
I had better
go back to the tent, Efendi Petrus.

586
01:38:10,676 --> 01:38:14,526
You'll get a reward if you tell him.

587
01:38:15,359 --> 01:38:19,679
I think it should be
you who will tell Nikola about it, David.

588
01:38:25,283 --> 01:38:29,283
Then I should go now.

589
01:38:55,494 --> 01:38:58,584
If we don't hear from the potter again...

590
01:38:59,621 --> 01:39:02,411
we know why.

591
01:39:04,067 --> 01:39:07,757
If he watches him...

592
01:39:09,977 --> 01:39:14,287
he may reach us soon.

593
01:39:16,297 --> 01:39:19,417
We're traders, Melik.

594
01:39:20,039 --> 01:39:23,249
Everyone can come to our workplace.

595
01:39:24,699 --> 01:39:27,989
His governors are leaving Nikola.

596
01:39:28,231 --> 01:39:32,381
Nikola's weakness won't endanger...

597
01:39:32,381 --> 01:39:36,381
our Holy father's passion for these lands.

598
01:39:37,519 --> 01:39:41,519
How will we do it?

599
01:39:43,174 --> 01:39:45,234
Like Osman did.

600
01:39:46,426 --> 01:39:47,926
With alliance.

601
01:39:48,360 --> 01:39:53,320
With Mongols, right?

602
01:39:54,811 --> 01:39:57,531
If I were Geyhatu...

603
01:39:58,490 --> 01:40:01,990
I wouldn't send my soldiers...

604
01:40:02,193 --> 01:40:08,083
without an ally.

605
01:40:08,734 --> 01:40:11,714
With whom they will ally?

606
01:40:12,296 --> 01:40:15,766
Do you think Nikola will do it?

607
01:40:16,046 --> 01:40:18,026
Osman is his greatest enemy.

608
01:40:18,438 --> 01:40:24,598
But it doesn't mean that
he'll let Geyhatu's people in.

609
01:40:25,390 --> 01:40:28,590
The governor that will replace Nikola...

610
01:40:29,265 --> 01:40:33,265
may collaborate.

611
01:40:34,517 --> 01:40:40,107
What if Osman finds out we're involved?

612
01:40:41,522 --> 01:40:43,372
What will we do then?

613
01:40:43,787 --> 01:40:47,607
We're not sure if he suspected us.

614
01:40:48,107 --> 01:40:53,317
Then we'll destroy his suspicions.

615
01:41:02,412 --> 01:41:03,572
How?

616
01:41:20,578 --> 01:41:24,848
- They're gone, sir.
- How?!

617
01:41:35,000 --> 01:41:37,480
We're here, Flatyos.

618
01:41:39,249 --> 01:41:42,849
- We're coming.
- Soldiers! Kill them!

619
01:41:42,924 --> 01:41:47,574
Allah is eternal!

620
01:42:04,939 --> 01:42:07,379
I'll kill you.

621
01:42:36,431 --> 01:42:38,941
I will kill you and your father here.

622
01:43:51,787 --> 01:43:53,317
Hold on, son!

623
01:44:15,883 --> 01:44:17,903
I'm here, brother.

624
01:44:18,071 --> 01:44:19,801
Brother!

625
01:44:46,852 --> 01:44:49,282
He's leaving!

626
01:44:55,318 --> 01:44:59,258
Come on Alps!

627
01:45:31,628 --> 01:45:33,548
Son!

628
01:45:33,783 --> 01:45:36,303
Are you okay?

629
01:45:44,776 --> 01:45:47,936
My Bamsı Bey. Is he okay?

630
01:45:48,479 --> 01:45:51,899
Yes, son. Don't worry.

631
01:45:55,881 --> 01:45:59,881
Thank Allah.

632
01:46:04,604 --> 01:46:08,184
I couldn't kill him, father.
I couldn't kill Flatyos.

633
01:46:12,054 --> 01:46:13,354
Brother.

634
01:46:13,449 --> 01:46:16,419
You are here in time.

635
01:46:25,725 --> 01:46:28,095
Where is Dumrul Alp?

636
01:46:49,320 --> 01:46:51,590
Thank you.

637
01:46:52,649 --> 01:46:55,859
I feel sorry for Aksu Sister.

638
01:46:56,276 --> 01:47:00,446
Her funeral was as nice as her.

639
01:47:07,234 --> 01:47:10,214
While she was trying to save me...

640
01:47:14,301 --> 01:47:16,211
What's wrong with you, Bala?

641
01:47:17,191 --> 01:47:22,291
You said I shouldn't come because of my
pain but you're the one with pain.

642
01:47:28,396 --> 01:47:30,916
You're sorry for Aksu Bacı.

643
01:47:31,836 --> 01:47:35,016
But there's something
else you're sorry for.

644
01:47:38,147 --> 01:47:39,147
Thank you.

645
01:47:39,159 --> 01:47:40,539
Come on.

646
01:47:40,716 --> 01:47:42,606
Eat.

647
01:47:44,140 --> 01:47:48,140
I'm angry with you.
You don't listen to me.

648
01:47:48,398 --> 01:47:51,058
Why are you here?

649
01:47:59,052 --> 01:48:01,862
May it be easy, Hatuns.

650
01:48:03,916 --> 01:48:06,376
Thank you, Hatun.

651
01:48:24,852 --> 01:48:26,982
What, Malhun Hatun?

652
01:48:28,281 --> 01:48:32,931
Yesterday, the Kayı Tent. Today, Söğüt.
Are you here to examine?

653
01:48:34,973 --> 01:48:37,903
I've heard about this soup kitchen.
I'm proud.

654
01:48:37,961 --> 01:48:40,691
I wanted to see it myself.

655
01:48:41,168 --> 01:48:43,658
So, you'll leave then.

656
01:48:45,361 --> 01:48:47,011
Mashallah.

657
01:48:47,824 --> 01:48:51,174
Muslims, non-Muslims...

658
01:48:53,256 --> 01:48:56,776
I'm happy that you love it.

659
01:49:00,466 --> 01:49:03,036
You said hard things to
Osman Bey yesterday.

660
01:49:03,704 --> 01:49:06,824
- He said nothing but...
- He is Bey, who is the son a Bey.

661
01:49:07,894 --> 01:49:10,514
I'm a daughter of a Bey.

662
01:49:11,369 --> 01:49:14,019
We've talked about the
future of our tents.

663
01:49:14,079 --> 01:49:16,689
And you've listened to us, obviously.

664
01:50:02,107 --> 01:50:06,547
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

665
01:50:25,631 --> 01:50:29,841
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

666
01:50:47,816 --> 01:50:49,416
My Sheik.

667
01:50:51,330 --> 01:50:55,680
You'll live here from now on.

668
01:50:59,433 --> 01:51:02,653
I know you want us to be comfortable.

669
01:51:03,374 --> 01:51:06,814
However, this comfort may
extend our way to go.

670
01:51:07,102 --> 01:51:12,902
The dervishes, the students and workers.

671
01:51:14,057 --> 01:51:18,057
They may stay here, we think.

672
01:51:19,655 --> 01:51:21,275
Come, please.

673
01:51:36,629 --> 01:51:40,049
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

674
01:51:58,548 --> 01:52:02,108
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

675
01:52:11,022 --> 01:52:13,662
We frequently say your name recently.

676
01:52:14,165 --> 01:52:17,335
May it be good, Inshallah.

677
01:52:18,620 --> 01:52:23,110
When Kayqubad came to Elbistan...

678
01:52:23,806 --> 01:52:27,096
he visited Dede Garkın...

679
01:52:27,171 --> 01:52:33,181
and he found him in a wreck then he felt
upset.

680
01:52:33,500 --> 01:52:36,360
He gave him a mansion.

681
01:52:36,538 --> 01:52:40,778
Just as Sultanu'l Ulema Bahattin...

682
01:52:41,141 --> 01:52:47,271
did to him during a visit to Konya.

683
01:52:48,799 --> 01:52:53,839
Who else can beg Allah like that?

684
01:52:54,374 --> 01:52:55,864
Both of them...

685
01:52:55,864 --> 01:53:03,043
said that staying with students in
Madrasah will be good for them.

686
01:53:05,352 --> 01:53:08,972
May Allah give us the way to follow him.

687
01:53:09,137 --> 01:53:12,437
Amin, my Sheik.

688
01:53:15,776 --> 01:53:21,366
This place will be full of the
voices of dervishes, Inshallah.

689
01:53:21,541 --> 01:53:25,541
Scribes and muftis who will
serve our holy state...

690
01:53:25,541 --> 01:53:29,541
will be raised here.

691
01:53:29,981 --> 01:53:35,081
If people have a problem, they
will come here.

692
01:53:37,230 --> 01:53:41,230
In the presence of scribes...

693
01:53:41,908 --> 01:53:45,678
soldiers and Beys will be equal.

694
01:53:52,846 --> 01:53:58,076
What the justice and the tradition
say will happen.

695
01:54:01,241 --> 01:54:05,601
What do you think, my Abdal?
Is the secret solved?

696
01:54:10,585 --> 01:54:14,585
You know every secret, my Pir.

697
01:54:20,916 --> 01:54:23,506
That's good, son.

698
01:54:24,417 --> 01:54:26,817
May Allah complete your intentions.

699
01:54:27,388 --> 01:54:32,118
If there's
no justice, the sky will collapse on us.

700
01:54:34,359 --> 01:54:40,169
A state's religion is justice, Ali said.

701
01:54:41,632 --> 01:54:45,512
- May Allah bless him.
- Amin.

702
01:55:09,402 --> 01:55:12,292
Where are you going, my Bey?

703
01:55:14,078 --> 01:55:16,408
It's time, Hatun.

704
01:55:18,450 --> 01:55:21,990
Will you do it in the tent?

705
01:55:23,552 --> 01:55:27,552
Do you think I'm novice?

706
01:55:29,462 --> 01:55:32,542
I know the potter is in Söğüt.

707
01:55:33,800 --> 01:55:37,890
I need to finish this.

708
01:55:38,994 --> 01:55:42,174
Inshaallah.

709
01:55:44,829 --> 01:55:47,959
Take care, my Bey.

710
01:55:48,878 --> 01:55:51,878
Don't worry.

711
01:56:03,634 --> 01:56:08,774
Making a sculpture
of a flawless face is hard.

712
01:56:10,919 --> 01:56:14,919
I think it's the best work I do.

713
01:56:16,315 --> 01:56:18,375
You're being unfair to yourself, Nikola.

714
01:56:18,375 --> 01:56:22,025
You're a great artist and a big commander.

715
01:56:23,349 --> 01:56:27,979
Yes, if we don't
count my failures against Osman.

716
01:56:36,549 --> 01:56:39,529
David wants to see you, sir.

717
01:56:40,270 --> 01:56:42,150
Let him in.

718
01:56:58,948 --> 01:57:01,638
Your wounds heal quickly.

719
01:57:01,892 --> 01:57:04,772
I think your father's prayers worked out.

720
01:57:04,842 --> 01:57:07,752
My wounds heal quickly.

721
01:57:07,938 --> 01:57:12,588
But what I'm
going to tell you will upset you.

722
01:57:13,465 --> 01:57:18,375
Yorgo accepted to collaborate with Osman.

723
01:57:24,165 --> 01:57:28,165
Isn't it such big news for a potter?

724
01:57:31,097 --> 01:57:34,837
Don't believe in everything you've heard.

725
01:57:37,548 --> 01:57:41,068
Osman said that himself.

726
01:57:42,443 --> 01:57:45,263
I thought you should know.

727
01:57:46,026 --> 01:57:47,806
Get out, David.

728
01:57:57,008 --> 01:58:01,008
Yorgo! Yorgo!

729
01:58:02,773 --> 01:58:05,063
I will host him here.

730
01:58:05,723 --> 01:58:09,723
Let's see if he appreciates
my art as you do.

731
01:59:02,131 --> 01:59:07,691
Your anger is my anger, your
revenge is my revenge.

732
01:59:09,337 --> 01:59:11,227
We'll take revenge on Nikola...

733
01:59:13,040 --> 01:59:16,400
who killed Targun and...

734
01:59:16,564 --> 01:59:18,934
spoiled our collaboration.

735
01:59:19,224 --> 01:59:24,554
We will, so that everyone will see what
it's like to play a trick on Cumans.

736
01:59:24,991 --> 01:59:29,461
We'll take Nikola's goods
and then kill him.

737
01:59:31,700 --> 01:59:36,680
We won't stop
until Targun's soul is in peace.

738
01:59:37,208 --> 01:59:44,208
Revenge! Revenge! Revenge!
Revenge! Revenge!

739
01:59:44,458 --> 01:59:55,448
Revenge! Revenge! Revenge!
Revenge! Revenge!

740
02:00:03,830 --> 02:00:07,670
We want to see our Osman Bey.

741
02:00:14,249 --> 02:00:17,049
My Bey. Merchant Melik wants to see you.

742
02:00:23,661 --> 02:00:25,791
Let him come.

743
02:00:51,584 --> 02:00:57,264
Tell me. What's that important?

744
02:01:00,219 --> 02:01:04,219
My Osman Bey...

745
02:01:04,336 --> 02:01:08,446
We trusted your word and...

746
02:01:09,059 --> 02:01:11,049
we brought a caravan.

747
02:01:12,745 --> 02:01:15,115
We kept our words...

748
02:01:15,655 --> 02:01:17,055
however...

749
02:01:19,333 --> 02:01:23,333
- why do you suspect my words?
- No, my Bey!

750
02:01:23,757 --> 02:01:28,877
However, as the time flies, we're at harm.

751
02:01:30,509 --> 02:01:32,439
Forgive us, my Bey.

752
02:01:33,317 --> 02:01:36,927
We dealt with so much.

753
02:01:38,094 --> 02:01:41,694
There are so many bandits around.

754
02:01:42,519 --> 02:01:46,519
However, even in Germiyans...

755
02:01:46,687 --> 02:01:49,347
in Chobanids...

756
02:01:49,726 --> 02:01:55,416
our waste is covered
with the courts, my Bey.

757
02:01:57,119 --> 02:02:01,589
- Who made you suspect my justice?
- No, my Bey.

758
02:02:01,640 --> 02:02:03,980
No...

759
02:02:04,451 --> 02:02:06,901
Then what do you want?

760
02:02:07,025 --> 02:02:10,515
We want a court, my Bey.

761
02:02:11,187 --> 02:02:14,317
However, we know that...

762
02:02:14,900 --> 02:02:17,660
you adjudge.

763
02:02:18,475 --> 02:02:19,605
However...

764
02:02:20,429 --> 02:02:23,639
you don't have any court or kadi.

765
02:02:37,065 --> 02:02:39,335
So, you want a court.

766
02:02:49,021 --> 02:02:52,151
You want a court...

767
02:02:55,876 --> 02:02:57,586
you...

768
02:02:59,345 --> 02:03:04,165
think my justice will appear late...

769
02:03:07,798 --> 02:03:10,188
as you please, then.

770
02:03:16,123 --> 02:03:18,593
The kadi of this court...

771
02:03:28,026 --> 02:03:31,196
is Sheik Edebalı.
- Thank you, my Bey.

772
02:03:31,385 --> 02:03:32,785
Thank you.

773
02:03:35,822 --> 02:03:37,472
If you excuse us.

774
02:04:08,268 --> 02:04:11,368
My Bey, the potter went to Governor
Nikola.

775
02:04:11,521 --> 02:04:14,091
He's coming to Söğüt now.

776
02:05:03,896 --> 02:05:06,276
May it be good.

777
02:05:07,119 --> 02:05:09,059
May it be good.

778
02:05:38,418 --> 02:05:40,738
We have martyrs!

779
02:05:51,767 --> 02:05:53,987
We have martyr!

780
02:05:54,314 --> 02:05:55,754
My son.

781
02:06:34,947 --> 02:06:39,507
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

782
02:06:41,570 --> 02:06:48,170
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

783
02:06:57,018 --> 02:07:01,818
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

784
02:08:04,536 --> 02:08:06,986
Osman Bey. Do you have time?

785
02:08:07,010 --> 02:08:09,480
We have things to talk.

786
02:08:27,098 --> 02:08:31,098
Not now, Malhun Hatun.
Not now.

787
02:08:33,799 --> 02:08:35,269
Alps!

788
02:08:56,059 --> 02:08:59,379
You didn't say anything about
my work of art, Yorgo.

789
02:09:04,042 --> 02:09:06,082
It's nice.

790
02:09:06,626 --> 02:09:08,236
Nice?

791
02:09:09,332 --> 02:09:11,912
Just nice?

792
02:09:14,604 --> 02:09:18,214
When you look at it, do you think it's
just nice?

793
02:09:22,315 --> 02:09:24,675
What else should I think?

794
02:09:28,883 --> 02:09:31,833
I'll tell you what to think.

795
02:09:51,332 --> 02:09:55,902
Can you see the anger of
a betrayed man, Yorgo?

796
02:10:04,892 --> 02:10:06,342
Look at it.

797
02:10:23,291 --> 02:10:26,361
Can you see it now?

798
02:10:28,836 --> 02:10:31,816
Look.
The same face expression.

799
02:10:33,269 --> 02:10:37,269
Can you see it?

800
02:10:38,237 --> 02:10:40,297
Look at it.

801
02:10:50,193 --> 02:10:52,623
Get this traitor out of here.

802
02:11:27,828 --> 02:11:29,778
The potter.

803
02:12:03,051 --> 02:12:04,311
Osman.

804
02:12:29,419 --> 02:12:31,959
You hosted Yorgo nicely, Nikola.

805
02:12:34,597 --> 02:12:39,237
He's unfaithful and he
doesn't know anything about art.

806
02:12:42,637 --> 02:12:44,017
Traitor.

807
02:12:45,779 --> 02:12:47,309
Flatyos.

808
02:12:47,739 --> 02:12:49,999
Do you know anything about art?

809
02:12:57,430 --> 02:13:01,430
It's from Constantinople, from
the Emperor.

810
02:13:14,145 --> 02:13:16,085
What does it say?

811
02:13:20,281 --> 02:13:22,571
He wants me there.

812
02:13:23,085 --> 02:13:24,825
In a short time.

813
02:13:26,790 --> 02:13:28,620
What does he want?

814
02:13:31,882 --> 02:13:34,092
Oh, my friend...

815
02:13:34,136 --> 02:13:36,686
The emperors just give orders.

816
02:13:36,941 --> 02:13:38,041
They don't...

817
02:13:40,860 --> 02:13:42,700
say why.

818
02:13:45,101 --> 02:13:47,661
As he wants me urgent...

819
02:13:47,698 --> 02:13:51,918
it means I won't have good days
in Constantinople.

820
02:14:14,409 --> 02:14:17,959
My Osman Bey... Forgive me.

821
02:14:20,231 --> 02:14:22,351
Spare my life, Osman Bey.

822
02:14:23,853 --> 02:14:26,073
I'll kill you.

823
02:14:28,095 --> 02:14:30,675
It'll be your gift.

824
02:14:32,499 --> 02:14:34,499
Whose dog are you?

825
02:14:34,863 --> 02:14:36,373
Who?

826
02:14:37,687 --> 02:14:39,637
Who do you work for?

827
02:14:39,944 --> 02:14:41,644
Tell me.

828
02:14:41,714 --> 02:14:42,834
Who?

829
02:14:43,124 --> 02:14:45,594
I'll tell you.

830
02:14:46,584 --> 02:14:48,694
I'll tell you everything.

831
02:14:49,421 --> 02:14:53,421
Those who try to betray you are the
ones who are close to you.

832
02:14:56,163 --> 02:14:58,593
Who?

833
02:14:59,706 --> 02:15:03,706
- Who are they?
- The one who betrays you is...

834
02:15:27,586 --> 02:15:55,366
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com